{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSix workflow files contain repeated, obvious, historical, or stale prose. Scope was revalidated on `origin/main@d6669496cae4`, including the new named Windows-lock proof in `test.yml`. Shortening comments must preserve trigger, permission, security, portability, and evidence contracts.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only allowlisted standalone comments and adjacent blank lines. Preserve workflow data, embedded shell, expressions, and behavior-bearing directives byte-for-byte. Replace narration with the minimum current rationale needed by each consumer.\n\n## Scope\n- `reconcile-bridge.yml` — Preserve copyable-client semantics; hourly/manual modes; Actions and ref-lock concurrency; full-history tickets worktree with merge-not-rebase/merge driver; job-local permissions; completed-pass-only 60-minute ceiling; pinned acli; temporary signing key/unsigned fallback; fail-loud no-op detection; default-off paced continuous chain with bounded failure handling; and conditional dimensionless CloudWatch metrics that never alter job outcome.\n- `release.yml` — Preserve dispatch-from-main authorization; version/registry/ancestry/environment/advisory guards; immutable pins; build-once artifacts with digest and baked-commit provenance; installed archive tests; exact-byte OIDC PyPI promotion; post-publish tag/release; publisher-digest verification before OIDC; bounded idempotent registry publish; evidence fragments; both `shellcheck disable=SC1091` directives; and the `zizmor` marker.\n- `structured-output-baseline.yml` — Preserve manual canonical-repository billable measurement; pre-call budget refusal; independent provider arms and secrets; Bedrock OIDC with both regions and step-confined exchange; external-test opt-in; provider overlays; 3600-second sweep bound; and always-uploaded unique raw results.\n- `terraform-drift.yml` — Preserve Terraform-path PR plus daily/manual triggers; independent fmt/plan jobs; plan-only OIDC; full-history checkout and current-tree assertion; Terraform 1.11.4 floor; validate-before-plan; detailed exit codes with `-lock=false`; advisory role outside Gerrit Verified; and the exact `mechanism-ok: ci_gate` marker.\n- `test.yml` — Preserve ordinary pushes excluding `feature/**`, `main`, and `tickets`; all PRs; six-hour/manual health; same-ref cancellation; shared Gerrit workflows; schedule-only mutation omission; clean-install path; soft last-green/bisect report; external self-skip behavior; breadth-tier distinctions; nonblocking link check; and the exact existing `predates-gate-ok` marker. For the named Windows exclusive-leg proof, condense the explanatory blocks before the `mechanism-ok` marker and between the step name and `continue-on-error`; preserve the complete `mechanism-ok: ci_gate` marker, if-present guard, bash shell, nonblocking disposition, placement before the default suite, and verbose platform-test command. Do not claim every trigger runs the full suite.\n- `verify-identity.yml` — Preserve config-driven advisory authentication and grandfathering; triggers/exclusions; full-history blobless checkout; temporary fail-closed pack limit with restoration; tickets worktree; ancestry-based key verification; object-database immutability; and config-driven op-cert verification without CI overrides.\n\nConsumers are GitHub Actions, Gerrit Verified, release and Terraform operators, PyPI/MCP Registry/GitHub Releases, Jira/tickets reconciliation, CloudWatch, and repository workflow-policy tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only allowlisted standalone comments or adjacent blank lines change in the six paths; workflow data, embedded shell, and directives remain exact.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and consumer has a concrete before/final PASS citation in a leaf-linked TSV authored by a reviewer who did not write the remediation.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and records `semantic-preservation=PASS` and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing or failing rows block closure.\n- [ ] The comment-only guard, directive census, focused workflow tests, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv repository gate pass.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded comment-only and exact-directive guards, focused workflow suites, path-scoped diff check, and worktree-venv lint. The independent TSV is authoritative for prose quality."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788624927013277001,"uuid":"03799d46-8633-4a26-8f4e-e0dc0a1c1f82"}